To use the Core ML framework on macOS to build and deploy machine learning models, you can follow these steps:

1. Install the Xcode development environment on your macOS machine.
2. Open the Xcode IDE and create a new project. Choose the "Single View App" template and name your project.
3. Add the Core ML framework to your project by selecting "File" > "Add Files to [project name]" and navigating to the "Frameworks" folder in the Xcode IDE.
4. Create a new Swift file for your Core ML model by selecting "File" > "New" > "File" and choosing the "Swift File" template. Name your file "CoreMLModel.swift".
5. Import the Core ML framework into your Swift file by adding the following line of code: "import CoreML"
6. Define your Core ML model in the Swift file. You can use the Core ML framework to create, train, and export your model. Here's an example of how to create a simple linear regression model:
```swift
import CoreML

class LinearRegression: MLModel {
    @objc dynamic var weights: [Double]
    @objc dynamic var bias: Double
}
```
7. Train your model using your data and export it as a .mlmodel file. You can use the Core ML framework to train your model and export it as a .mlmodel file. Here's an example of how to train a simple linear regression model:
```swift
let model = LinearRegression()
